<title>GERMANY: Viag says BT alliance continues.</title>
<headline>Viag says BT alliance continues.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Viag AG said on Wednesday it would go ahead with plans to make a joint application with British Telecom for Germany's E2 mobile telephone network despite the announcement by RWE AG that it would pull out.</p>
<p>The company said in a regulatory news release that it would apply for the licence at the appropriate time.</p>
<p>&quot;The telecommunications strategy of Viag and BT will continue unchanged without the entry of RWE into the alliance,&quot; the news release said.</p>
<p>RWE and Veba AG said separately they were in the final stages of cooperation talks together with Cable &amp; Wireless.</p>
<p>-- Douglas Busvine, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
